+## Configuration contract (task-mandated names — keep exactly)
+
+| Env var | Use |
+| --- | --- |
+| `PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID` | Server: `oauth2.clientId`. Browser: exposed via `GET /api/paypal/config` (client id only — rule 12). |
+| `PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET` | Server only: `oauth2.clientSecret`. Never sent to the browser, never logged. |
+| `PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID` | Server only: `webhook_id` in verify-webhook-signature body. |
+| `PAYPAL_API_BASE` | Default `https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com`. Passed to the SDK as `serverOptions: { baseUrl: PAYPAL_API_BASE }` (this SDK declares exactly one environment, emits no `ServerEnvironment`; any other host is a `serverOptions.baseUrl` override — `src/servers.ts`: `options.serverOptions?.baseUrl`). The SDK's OAuth token request follows the same base URL, so it also goes to `PAYPAL_API_BASE`. Trailing slash stripped for the hand-built webhook/token URLs. |
+| `PAYPAL_ENV` | `"sandbox"` or `"live"` — chooses **only** the browser script URL (`https://www.sandbox.paypal.com/web-sdk/v6/core` vs `https://www.paypal.com/web-sdk/v6/core`). Never inferred from `PAYPAL_API_BASE` (harness points it at a local proxy). Unknown value at shop startup = fail loudly, not silent default. |
+| `PAYPAL_TEST_BUYER_COUNTRY` | Sandbox only: browser `testBuyerCountry`. Unset ⇒ the key is **not sent** at all. Never sent in live. |
+
+Client built **once** in the `lib/paypal.js` factory (long-lived: resource getters are memoized and
+the OAuth2 token cache lives on it; there is no `close()`), held by `server.js` startup and injected
+into `createApp`. Construction:
+
+```
+new PaypalClient({
+  oauth2: { clientId, clientSecret },              // both required: factory throws naming the missing var, never echoes values
+  serverOptions: { baseUrl: apiBase },             // PAYPAL_API_BASE override (see above)
+  fetch: fetchImpl,                                // injection seam for tests; global fetch in production
+  retry: { timeout: 30_000 },                      // per attempt; POSTs stay outside httpMethodsToRetry (default), GET getOrder keeps default retries
+  logging: { level: "off" },                       // explicit: stops PAYPAL_CLIENT_LOG arming logging from outside; logRequestBody stays off (bodies carry payer/order data)
+})
+```
+
+No per-call `logging` level is ever passed (it would turn request-body logging on for that call).
