+## Operations in scope (from `map/operations/orders.md` — one pass)
+
+All: resource `client.orders`, auth `oauth2`, flat channel-blind request object, `ApiPromise<T,E>`,
+awaited (throwing mode). The SDK mints a fresh `Idempotency-Key` per non-GET call (invisible, not
+settable); retries of one call reuse it, a new call mints a new one — hence the explicit
+`PayPal-Request-Id` rows below.
+
+### 1. `createOrder` — `POST /v2/checkout/orders`
+- Signature: `createOrder(request: Orders.CreateOrderRequest, options?): ApiPromise<Order, Orders.CreateOrderError>`
+- Request fields: `body: OrderRequest` (body, **required**); headers all optional:
+  `payPalMockResponse` (`PayPal-Mock-Response`), `payPalRequestId` (`PayPal-Request-Id`),
+  `payPalPartnerAttributionId`, `payPalClientMetadataId`, `prefer` (`Prefer`, default
+  `"return=minimal"`), `payPalAuthAssertion`.
+- `OrderRequest` (`src/models/order-request.ts`): `intent: CheckoutPaymentIntent` **required**
+  (`CheckoutPaymentIntent.Capture === "CAPTURE"`); `purchaseUnits: PurchaseUnitRequest[]`
+  **required**; `processingInstruction?`, `payer?`, `paymentSource?`, `applicationContext?` optional.
+- `PurchaseUnitRequest` (`src/models/purchase-unit-request.ts`): `amount: AmountWithBreakdown`
+  **required**; `customId?` (wire `custom_id`), `invoiceId?`, `items?: ItemRequest[]`, rest optional.
+  `AmountWithBreakdown`: `currencyCode: string`, `value: string`, `breakdown?`
+  (`AmountBreakdown.itemTotal?: Money`). `Money`: `currencyCode`, `value` (decimal **string**).
+  `ItemRequest`: `name: string`, `unitAmount: Money`, `quantity: string` required; `sku?` optional.
+- Returns `Order` (`src/models/order.ts`): every member optional (`id?`, `status?`, `purchaseUnits?`…)
+  — a truncated 2xx decodes cleanly, so **assert `order.id !== undefined` after the call**; missing
+  id on a write = outcome unknown, never success.
+- Error arms (`Orders.CreateOrderError`, body model `Error` for every arm — `Error`
+  (`src/models/error.ts`): `name: string`, `message: string`, `debugId: string` (wire `debug_id`),
+  `details?: ErrorDetails[]` (`issue: string` required, `description?`, `field?`…)):
+  `"error"` [400] · `"error2"` [401] · `"error3"` [422] · `"error4"` [default] · `"undeclared"`
+  [default-matched body that did not fit]. Arm tags are schema-derived, **not** statuses — code reads
+  `err.status` and extracts reason text from `err.payload.body` (`message` + `details[].issue/description`), never switches on `payload.kind` across operations.
+
+### 2. `captureOrder` — `POST /v2/checkout/orders/{id}/capture`
+- Signature: `captureOrder(request: Orders.CaptureOrderRequest, options?): ApiPromise<Order, Orders.CaptureOrderError>`
+- Fields: `id` (path, required); optional headers `payPalMockResponse`, `payPalRequestId`, `prefer`
+  (default `"return=minimal"`), `payPalClientMetadataId`, `payPalAuthAssertion`; `body?: OrderCaptureRequest`
+  (only member `paymentSource?` — nothing requires it, but the body itself must be sent as an empty
+  object `{}`, see 1b.3: the real sandbox rejects a bodiless capture with `415 UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE`).
+- Returns `Order`. Payment facts live at
+  `purchaseUnits[].payments.captures[]: OrdersCapture` (`src/models/orders-capture.ts`):
+  `status?: CaptureStatus` (`Completed === "COMPLETED"`, `Pending === "PENDING"`, `Declined`, …),
+  `id?`, `amount?: Money`, `customId?` (wire `custom_id`).
+- Error arms: `"error"` [400] · `"error2"` [401] · `"error3"` [403] · `"error4"` [404] · `"error5"`
+  [422] · `"error6"` [500] · `"error7"` [default] · `"undeclared"`. A 422's reason is read from
+  `details[].issue` (`INSTRUMENT_DECLINED`, `ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED`, `TRANSACTION_REFUSED`, …).
+
+### 3. `getOrder` — `GET /v2/checkout/orders/{id}`
+- Signature: `getOrder(request: Orders.GetOrderRequest, options?): ApiPromise<Order, Orders.GetOrderError>`
+- Fields: `id` (path, required); `fields?`, `payPalMockResponse?`, `payPalAuthAssertion?` optional — none set.
+- Error arms: `"error"` [401] · `"error2"` [404] · `"error3"` [default] · `"undeclared"`.
+- Used to settle unknown capture outcomes and `ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED` (rule 10), and to verify a
+  capture from webhook data when needed. GET is inside the default retry gate — acceptable for a read.
+
+### Not in the SDK — webhook verification (Blocker resolved, see Assumptions)
+The SDK has **no webhook surface at all** (no operation, no verifier — confirmed: no webhook mention
+in `sdk-map.md`/`map/`; `typescript-client-initialization`: "There is no webhook surface at all … on
+any generated TypeScript SDK"). Hardening rule 6 mandates exactly:
+`POST {PAYPAL_API_BASE}/v1/notifications/verify-webhook-signature` with a client-credentials token.
+So this one call (plus its token fetch `POST {PAYPAL_API_BASE}/v1/oauth2/token`,
+`Authorization: Basic base64(clientId:clientSecret)`, form `grant_type=client_credentials`) is made
+with the **same injected `fetch`** directly against `PAYPAL_API_BASE` — the only server-side PayPal
+REST calls not going through the SDK, because the SDK cannot make them. All Orders calls go through
+the SDK without exception. Token cached in-module until shortly before `expires_in`.
+
+## Server surface to build
+
+| Route | Behaviour |
+| --- | --- |
+| `GET /api/paypal/config` | `{ clientId, scriptUrl, env, currency: "USD", ...(sandbox && PAYPAL_TEST_BUYER_COUNTRY ? { testBuyerCountry } : {}) }`. No secret, no webhook id. |
+| `POST /api/paypal/orders` | Body `{ items, email? }` only — prices/totals/currency from the browser are ignored (`priceCart` re-prices from SKUs+qty; rule 1/11). Creates the shop order (claim, pending, method `paypal`), then SDK `createOrder`. Returns `{ id, orderId }` (`id` = PayPal order id the browser session needs, `orderId` = shop order id). On PayPal refusal the shop order is marked failed and table 1b.4 applies. |
+| `POST /api/paypal/orders/:paypalOrderId/capture` | Browser sends only the PayPal order id (path). Shop order located by stored PayPal order id (invariant below). Capture via SDK, verify, settle (rules 4/5/8/10). Returns shop order status. Declined instrument ⇒ 422 with PayPal's reason, order stays **pending** (buyer may pick another method and click again). |
+| `POST /api/paypal/webhooks` | Raw event JSON. Verify first (rule 6); non-`SUCCESS` ⇒ 400, nothing changes. Then dedupe by event id (rule 7). Only `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED` can pay (verify amount/currency/custom_id against the bound shop order, settle atomically); `CHECKOUT.ORDER.APPROVED` and everything else never pay and never move an order backwards (rules 4/9). Answer 200 after recording. |
+
+Amount conversion lives in one function in `lib/paypal.js`:
+`centsToPayPalAmount(cents)`: integer cents → decimal string (`4900 → "49.00"`, `5 → "0.05"`),
+plus `payPalAmountToCents(value)` for verifying amounts coming back (strict
+`^\d+(\.\d{1,2})?$` parse, no floats). Currency sent as `"USD"` (PayPal wire form of the shop's
+`"usd"`); item breakdown `item_total` equals the total and per-item `unit_amount × quantity` sums
+to it (rule 2).
+
+"Paid" verification (capture response, `getOrder` settle, and webhook capture alike — one shared
+`settleFromPayPalOrder`/capture-check used by all paths): a capture exists with
+`status === "COMPLETED"`, `amount.value` parses to exactly the shop order's `total_cents`,
+`amount.currencyCode` equals USD (case-insensitive), and the purchase unit's / capture's
+`custom_id` equals the shop order id. Then claim the paid transition atomically (1b.1) and fulfil
+only if the claim won.
+
+## 1b.1 DURABLE WRITES
+
+DUPLICATE CLAIMS
+
+| Write | Where the claim is stored | What rejects the second one | Where that rejection is caught | Where in the code |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `createOrder` | The shop order row itself, inserted `pending` in `orders` **before** the SDK call (`lib/db.js:createOrder`); its id is sent as `purchase_units[0].custom_id`, `invoice_id`, and the `PayPal-Request-Id` header, and the returned PayPal order id is stored on the row under a **UNIQUE index** on `orders.paypal_order_id` | The UNIQUE index on `paypal_order_id` refuses binding a second shop order to the same PayPal order; the `PayPal-Request-Id` (= shop order id, a value every retry of *this* shop order computes identically) makes a re-sent create return the original PayPal order instead of a second one | `setPayPalOrderId` catches the SQLite `UNIQUE constraint` message and rethrows with `code = "PAYPAL_ORDER_ALREADY_BOUND"`; the create handler maps that code to 409 | `lib/db.js:setPayPalOrderId`, `server.js` `POST /api/paypal/orders`; test: "the same PayPal order cannot be bound to two shop orders" |
+| `captureOrder` | Row in `paypal_capture_claims (order_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, paypal_order_id, claimed_at)` inserted before the SDK call, keyed by shop order id; the claim's reference is sent as the capture `PayPal-Request-Id` | The PRIMARY KEY refuses the second claim insert | `tryClaimCapture` uses `INSERT OR IGNORE` and returns `changes === 1`; the loser does **not** call capture again — it polls the order status while the winner settles, and on timeout settles from `getOrder` (below) / reports the order's current status | `lib/db.js:tryClaimCapture`/`releaseCaptureClaim`, `server.js` `POST /api/paypal/orders/:paypalOrderId/capture` claim loop; test: "capture verifies amount/custom_id and fulfils exactly once; second and concurrent captures are safe" |
+| Webhook-driven settlement (`PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED`) | Row in `webhook_events (id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, event_type, received_at)` inserted before acting on the event | The PRIMARY KEY refuses a repeat delivery's insert | `recordWebhookEvent` returning "already seen" (constraint caught by code, not message) ⇒ handler answers 200 and changes nothing | `lib/db.js:recordWebhookEvent`, `server.js` `POST /api/paypal/webhooks`; test: "PENDING capture waits; the CAPTURE.COMPLETED webhook settles it once, replays change nothing" |
+
+Claim release: a capture claim is deleted when PayPal **refuses** the capture (an `ApiError`
+4xx/422 — the request reached PayPal and was rejected, e.g. `INSTRUMENT_DECLINED`), when the
+capture outcome is `PENDING`, and after an unknown outcome once the `getOrder` re-read has been
+attempted — so a later attempt with another instrument is not blocked. Re-capture stays safe
+after release because the retry sends the same capture `PayPal-Request-Id`
+(`capture-<shopOrderId>`) and fulfilment is separately guarded by the atomic paid transition.
+Fulfil-once is separately guaranteed by the atomic paid transition:
+`UPDATE orders SET status='paid', … WHERE id=? AND status='pending'` — fulfil only when exactly
+one row changed; the loser (second capture, racing webhook, replay) sees the already-paid/fulfilled
+order and changes nothing (rules 8/9).
+
+UNKNOWN OUTCOMES
+
+| Write | The operation you re-read with | The reference you search by | Where in the code | The test that fails the connection |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `captureOrder` | `getOrder` | The PayPal order id bound to the shop order (`orders.paypal_order_id`, also the capture path id) | `lib/paypal.js:translatePayPalError` (connection/timeout on a write → `unknown`), `server.js` capture-route `catch` → `paypalService.getOrder` → `settleFromPayPalOrder` | "a lost capture connection is settled by re-reading, never reported as failed" (asserts the `getOrder` request was made) |
+| `createOrder` | No re-read exists: the SDK offers no lookup of an order by `PayPal-Request-Id`/`custom_id` (no list/search operation for orders). Settlement instead re-sends nothing and relies on the claim: the pending shop order + its `PayPal-Request-Id` mean a buyer retry creates no payment; outcome reported as unknown (502), never "failed", and the pending order is left for the buyer/webhook to settle — see Assumptions. A `DecodeError` on a 2xx (id unreadable) is treated the same way. | Shop order id sent as `PayPal-Request-Id` / `custom_id` | `lib/paypal.js:translatePayPalError`, `server.js` `POST /api/paypal/orders` `unknown` branch (502, order left `pending`) | "a lost create connection leaves the order pending (unknown), with exactly one create sent" |
+
+Never-sent failures get their own outcome and **no** re-read: `AuthError` (credential could not be
+obtained) and `EncodeError` (value would not encode) on either write ⇒ 502 fixed message
+("our credentials" / integration fault), claim released for capture (nothing reached PayPal),
+asserted by a second test per write (bad-credentials token refusal ⇒ no `getOrder` request follows).
+
+## 1b.2 CROSS-OPERATION INVARIANTS
+
+| Invariant | Where the legal set comes from | Enforced where | The test that proves it |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| A PayPal order id presented for capture must be bound to exactly one shop order | This application's `orders` table (`paypal_order_id` UNIQUE), read before any claim or capture call | Capture route: `getOrderByPayPalId` lookup; unknown id ⇒ 404, **capture never called** | Capture with an unbound PayPal order id ⇒ 404 and the faked fetch records no capture request |
+| The `custom_id` on the captured purchase unit / capture must equal that shop order's id, and captured amount+currency must equal the shop order total | The bound shop order row (server-priced total) | Shared settle check used by capture response, `getOrder` settle, and webhook paths, before the atomic paid claim | Faked capture returning a wrong amount or wrong `custom_id` ⇒ order stays pending, no shipment |
+| Webhook `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED`: `resource.custom_id` (when present) names the shop order and `supplementary_data.related_ids.order_id` (when present) names its bound PayPal order | The bound shop order row | Webhook handler after verification + dedupe | Verified event whose amount/custom_id disagrees ⇒ 200 recorded, order unchanged |
+| SKUs/quantities in a create request must be catalog SKUs with integer qty 1..10 | `lib/catalog.js` via `priceCart` (existing enforcement) | Create route before the shop-order claim is inserted (a rejected bag leaves no claim behind) | Unknown SKU / qty 0 / 1.5 / 11 ⇒ 400, no PayPal create request recorded |
+
