+`captureOrder` (`Orders.CaptureOrderRequest`):
+
+| Field | What requires it | Set it? |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `payPalRequestId` | The DUPLICATE CLAIMS row for captureOrder (claim reference) | ✅ set it from that row |
+| `prefer` | Rule 4: capture response must carry `payments.captures[]` (status/amount/custom_id) to verify before marking paid | ✅ `"return=representation"` |
+| `body` (`OrderCaptureRequest.paymentSource?`) | Real PayPal sandbox (harness, order `9JF068826A073763J`): a capture with the body omitted carries no body and no `Content-Type` (SDK `map/operations/orders.md`: “omit it and the request carries no body and no `Content-Type` header at all”) and is rejected `415 UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE` (“The request payload is not supported”, debug id `f6507972aed1f`), leaving the shop order pending/unfulfilled. PayPal's real answer wins over the earlier “omit entirely” assumption. | ✅ set it to `{}` (empty object — SDK then sends `Content-Type: application/json` and `"{}"`); `paymentSource` inside it stays unset |
