+The test that proves it: faked-fetch tests parse the actual request the SDK sent (headers + body)
+for create and capture and assert the exact key set — no `PayPal-Mock-Response`, no invented
+headers/fields beyond SDK-sent ones (`Authorization`, `Content-Type`, SDK identity headers and its
+minted `Idempotency-Key` are the SDK's own, not ours).
