+## 1b.4 WHEN THE API SAYS NO (per operation, caller = browser hitting our routes)
+
+`createOrder` (via `POST /api/paypal/orders`) and `captureOrder` (via capture route) share the ladder;
+`getOrder` only surfaces inside settlement:
+
+| status | your app answers | the caller reads | test |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| a `4xx` other than 401/403/429 | the same `4xx` | the API's reason text from `err.payload` (`Error.message` + `details[].issue/description`, joined, length-capped) — logged **and** returned | fake a 422 with a reason; assert the reason is in our response |
+| 401 / 403 | 502 | fixed message — our credentials | fake a 401; assert 502 and the fixed message |
+| 429 | 503 | fixed message — our quota | fake a 429; assert 503 |
+| 5xx | 502 | fixed message | fake a 500; assert 502 |
+| no response, on a write | per UNKNOWN OUTCOMES (capture: settle via `getOrder`; create: unknown, order left pending) | unknown — never "failed" | connection-failure tests in 1b.1 |
+| no response, on a read (`getOrder` inside settle) | 502 | fixed message; outcome stays unknown, order unchanged | settle test where the re-read also fails |
+| `DecodeError` on 2xx | unknown (write may have taken effect) — settle like no-response | unknown | stub a malformed 2xx body; assert not marked paid/failed |
+| capture 422 `INSTRUMENT_DECLINED` (rule 5) | 422 | PayPal's reason + "choose another way to pay"; order stays pending, capture claim released | mock-response-style 422 body via faked fetch; assert pending, no shipment, second attempt allowed |
+| capture 422 `ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED` (rule 10) | settle via `getOrder`, then 200 if verified paid | order status | already-captured test asserting the `getOrder` request was made |
+
+Webhook route is not caller-data-driven in this sense: verification failure ⇒ 400 and nothing
+changes; verified but unpayable/duplicate/out-of-order events ⇒ 200, recorded once, nothing changes.
+
+## Enum / model facts relied on
+
+- `CheckoutPaymentIntent.Capture === "CAPTURE"`; `CaptureStatus.Completed === "COMPLETED"`,
+  `Pending === "PENDING"` (open enums — compare against members, unknown values round-trip).
+- Capture status `PENDING` (rule 5): order stays pending, no fulfilment; the later
+  `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED` webhook settles it.
+- `Error` model aliasing: the SDK exports a model type named `Error` — never imported unaliased in
+  this JS project (no SDK type imports at all; shapes are followed from this sheet).
+- `.asApiResult()` is **not** used: no in-scope operation resolves to `undefined`, and no success
+  status/headers are needed — awaited mode plus the error ladder covers everything (mode chosen at
+  write time, per operation).
+- No pagination, no streaming in scope; `ClientOptions.fetch` is the only transport seam (used for
+  test injection). SDK server-side only — never in the browser.
+
+## Browser plan (Web SDK v6 — from `heistproof:paypal-web-sdk-v6`)
+
+- Server supplies config via `GET /api/paypal/config` (above). Page loads the env-correct v6 core
+  script once, `onload` bootstraps.
+- `window.paypal.createInstance({ clientId, components: ["paypal-payments", "venmo-payments", "paypal-messages"], pageType: "checkout", ...(testBuyerCountry ? { testBuyerCountry } : {}) })`,
+  `sdk.findEligibleMethods({ currencyCode: "USD" })`; show only eligible
+  `<paypal-button>` / `<venmo-button>` / `<paypal-pay-later-button>` (hidden until eligible; Pay Later
+  button gets `productCode`/`countryCode` from `methods.getDetails("paylater")`).
+- One session per method (`createPayPalOneTimePaymentSession` / `createVenmoOneTimePaymentSession` /
+  `createPayLaterOneTimePaymentSession`) with shared handlers: `onApprove` POSTs our capture route
+  (server decides paid), `onCancel`/`onError` only show a message. Click handler calls
+  `createOrder()` **without awaiting before** `session.start({ presentationMode: "auto" }, createOrderPromise)`
+  (transient activation). Browser sends only SKUs+quantities.
+- Pay Later messaging: `<paypal-message amount currency-code="USD" auto-bootstrap>` via
+  `sdk.createPayPalMessages()`, `amount` updated as a decimal string on every `bag:change`.
+- If PayPal is unconfigured/unreachable the card form keeps working untouched.
+
+## Assumptions & Blockers
+
+- **Blocker (resolved):** SDK has no webhook-verify operation — resolved by the mandated direct
+  `POST {PAYPAL_API_BASE}/v1/notifications/verify-webhook-signature` (hardening rule 6), the sole
+  non-SDK PayPal REST call; flagged here rather than silently violating "every call via the SDK".
+- **Blocker (noted, mitigated):** an unknown-outcome `createOrder` cannot be re-read by reference
+  through this SDK (no order search). Mitigation is the claim + `PayPal-Request-Id` + leaving the
+  order pending (1b.1) — no payment can be taken from an unapproved order, so nothing can be
+  wrongly fulfilled from this path.
+- Minor: shop currency is USD-only (`priceCart` returns `"usd"`); email on PayPal orders is
+  accepted and stored on the shop order exactly as the card flow does.
+- Minor: no credentials exist while building — no smoke call against real PayPal is possible or
+  attempted; faked-fetch tests are the verification. Harness runs sandbox afterwards.
+- Smoke of in-scope operations against a real credential: **skipped** (no credentials exist, per
+  task) — not a silent omission.
+
+## REQUIRED READING
+
+| Step | Skill |
+| --- | --- |
+| Error ladder at every call site (family narrowed on `err.kind`, arms per operation, rethrow outside-family) | MUST load `paypal:typescript-error-handling` ✅ loaded |
+| Client construction, once-only lifetime, base-URL override, missing-credential startup check | MUST load `paypal:typescript-client-initialization` ✅ loaded |
+| OAuth2 client-credentials wiring, token cache, `AuthError` semantics | MUST load `paypal:typescript-authentication` ✅ loaded |
+| Flat request objects, defaults sent, `ApiPromise` modes | MUST load `paypal:typescript-calling-endpoints` ✅ loaded |
+| Model required/optional members, open enums, money-as-string | MUST load `paypal:typescript-models` ✅ loaded |
+| Retry policy, logging posture, `fetch` seam, base-URL capture at construction | MUST load `paypal:typescript-configuration-resilience` ✅ loaded |
+| Faked `fetch` through `ClientOptions.fetch`, wire-shaped stubs, token-request-first | MUST load `paypal:typescript-testing` ✅ loaded |
+| Browser buttons, sessions, Pay Later messaging | MUST load `heistproof:paypal-web-sdk-v6` ✅ loaded |
+| Attack rules 1–12 | MUST load `heistproof:checkout-hardening` ✅ loaded |
+
+All fixed-floor skills (`typescript-error-handling`, `typescript-client-initialization`,
+`typescript-testing`) and every skill named above were loaded before implementation.
